window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b><i>Birdie</i></b></p> <p>I’m not sure if it was the thrill of the lust, his mind-blowing scent, or because of my loneliness, but I claimed a man who I thought was a breathtaking stranger. Turns out the tall, jaw-droppingly gorgeous wolf shifter is <i>my childhood best friend, </i>Sebastian Tucker.</p> <p>Even though I’m hesitant to seal the mating bond, mainly because he’s six years younger than me, there’s something utterly desirable about him. Not only is the sexual attraction between us so hot it’s almost scandalous, Sebastian makes me feel confident, encouraging my passions and my personality, allowing me to truly be myself.</p> <p><i>The boy I once knew and loved as a friend is becoming the man I’m quickly falling for.</i></p> <p><b><i>Sebastian</i></b></p> <p>The pain of thinking I would never see the love of my life again when she moved away was unbearable, but fate intervened when we crossed paths at the tree farm where I work. Even though she didn’t recognize me, Birdie McGee made my lifelong dreams a reality when she <i>claimed</i> <i>me as her mate</i>, and that’s a huge deal in the shifter world.</p> <p>Her hypnotic scent seeping into my lungs verifies her lust for me, but our age gap may be the reason she’s hesitant. If Birdie leaves me again, she will forever wound my heart, but I’m willing to sacrifice everything for the chance.</p> <p><i>We only have one thing left to seal the mating bond, and I’ve never been more ready to be bitten by my one true love.</i></p>"; 
